          "question": "Does his age change what is recommended?",
          "answer": "I could not find an answer to this in the material I searched. None of the retrieved documents covers how a child's age changes asthma diagnosis or treatment. The asthma guidance (\"Asthma: confirming the diagnosis and the stepwise approach to controller therapy\", guideline-asthma-diagnosis-and-stepwise-therapy) describes the diagnosis in general terms. It says a diagnosis needs a matching pattern of symptoms and evidence of changing airflow. It does not say how that changes for a four-year-old. The other documents in the search are about blood pressure, anxiety, urinary infections and flu, so they do not help here.\n\nThe asthma guidance also says a normal breathing test on a good day does not rule asthma out.\n\nPlease ask his doctor or nurse directly whether his age changes how he is assessed or treated. Any treatment decision should be made with a clinician who has examined him. Do not start, stop or change any medicine based on this.\n\nIf he is struggling to breathe, his lips or face look blue or grey, he cannot speak in full sentences, or he is getting worse quickly, seek emergency care now.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
